{"posts":[{"id":"quasimodo_p35_851","t":"Nice one. I think you're onto something there. i've been looking at that also after you pointed it out. Well Done","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#851","p":35,"im":[],"m":851},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_852","t":"This could be a right structure for the formation of a Qm?\n\nupload","a":"matteo","d":"","n":"#852","p":35,"im":[],"m":852},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_853","t":"Looks like it could be a nice setup.","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#853","p":35,"im":[],"m":853},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_854","t":"astro wrote: Nice one. I think you're onto something there. i've been looking at that also after you pointed it out. Well Done\n\nThanks astro, I find that really encouraging!\n\nmatteo wrote: This could be a right structure for the formation of a Qm?\n\nI saw those engulfing too matteo, Could be a QM, Would you take this trade?","a":"projectsagana","d":"","n":"#854","p":35,"im":[],"m":854},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_855","t":"matteo wrote: This could be a right structure for the formation of a Qm?\n\nHi Matteo and welcome, please don't use external image hosts. for some reason i cant zoom that picture when clicking on it\n\nhere are some instruction on image attachments readthemarket.com/index.php/forum/welcom...0-charts-attachments","a":"Harry","d":"","n":"#855","p":35,"im":[],"m":855},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_856","t":"QMs can look like this too. I didn't spot it until now!","a":"projectsagana","d":"","n":"#856","p":35,"im":[],"m":856},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_857","t":"Any one saw this QM too","a":"projectsagana","d":"","n":"#857","p":35,"im":[],"m":857},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_858","t":"Sorry not being with you that much those months. Had a car accident and then my wife quit so feel a bit depress. 1rst trades since a long time. I should recover soon ( maybe 1 or 2 years)\n\nQm again","a":"mertch","d":"","n":"#858","p":35,"im":["cb222bd398e45972a5ff566ded664c9c77db8275"],"m":858},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_859","t":"Hi guys, havent posted for a while but been working away. As soon as I've got everything sorted in my head I'll resume my journal. I've read this whole thread and I have a few questions that I dont think have been asked before.\n\nSo I'm watching price as it approaches the zone waiting for it to make a lower low, followed by a higher high (which breaches the high preceding the low) which it eventually does. so I think I'm looking at teh start of a QM. But where to place an order? Usually you have some visual looking H+S level that normally works but its not that clear here. Should I be placing an order at the first \"low\" on the left? It seems that from reading other parts of the forum that if I do this, then I still need to have my stop below the zone rather than the low in case PA turns into a diamond. The problem here is that the HTF demand I'm seeing comes from hourly/4hour, yet this QM I'm looking at is 5 minute so the zone is enormous compared to the relative 5 min PA.\n\nSo for this I'm thinking that if its hourly demand zone, I should probably only consider a 15/30min QM, if its a 30 minute demand zone then 5/15 QM is ok, but if I'm looking at 1min PA, there needs to be a 5/15minute demand/supply zone.\n\nThere's obviously no point on looking at a 1 min QM setup as a way to trade a daily demand zone but does anyone have any rules as to what timeframe a QM is acceptable to consider vs a relative s/d zone? Any feedback on this train of thought would be much appreciated!","a":"superMAD","d":"","n":"#859","p":35,"im":["fad367ce6039704bdc8efc950127d259ea30a1ff"],"m":859},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_861","t":"","a":"mertch","d":"","n":"#861","p":35,"im":["8d9724c9784dcc3f11b1c3deb88b4852e5cf9061"],"m":861},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_862","t":"On the first QM the second shoulder is slightly higher than the left, does that negate the formation? thanks","a":"aus1way","d":"","n":"#862","p":35,"im":["7d898a248ac25599395d01c09709af295198c660"],"m":862},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_863","t":"I would consider is a valid QM, although some may not. I love QM's","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#863","p":35,"im":[],"m":863},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_864","t":"That's my 20 QM... suggestions will be appreciated!!!","a":"juniormaiafx","d":"","n":"#864","p":35,"im":["3db79cfe386fb4dd70642689a2f6db3fe1ad724e","5bcbae33a766fb672991ad088c1fbeebb145a5b7","da0f6bf847cec13822d8139a3597e010c173b500","36a5ad93d61f693711d426382d832bb7f3c6d97a","1623297ef4cc1dc0e2677f8fc1f10558df1ea1a0","cdcb469dc5b4999a25ffe433d30002d2743a95df","d42429a89ab4397549fb0102cad946685b521c6f","2505b9e1de4cf026c7bb8b2361060c77d84c36f1","ba50162d155770a3d288a2b3fdeda735a683d53a","24c1c3917687be9c7b838dab0ecd56a8285f8406","7983a4a4d8559a29e9b169dbe303838ee1c5cbcd","9f89931d1b2affdf0303a536f82e6c86b0306867","940c10bb1715a0b2462bf5943c92bc16385ce9e5","b2fb7833039b4cc18e50e3fdfbf153f33fe475e2","0841c0abb06842f20a0de1a03071945dcf2f902d","15010925daf0d379dab360331a18f9302aca34c2","363034b9adf9aa661742d44e6602ff38cf2090a8","69a247c7d09f546f5015910bd399c963aaeee9e4","38c398776a76b5c9a63b2d5d83fbeecd8d687fa7"],"m":864},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_865","t":"Nice QMs juniormaiafx! I also like how you labeled where the QMs occured!","a":"projectsagana","d":"","n":"#865","p":35,"im":[],"m":865},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_866","t":"I agree, Excellent QM examples JnrMFX.\n\nThe only 1 I would question is your\n\nvery first one. It looks like it may be a reaction to FL, rather than the QM level.","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#866","p":35,"im":["a639d21d2d766661ed83c3c0b4c97ef4090bdd16"],"m":866},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_867","t":"Hi Juniormaiafx\n\nNice QM examples!\n\nIn some of your charts you questioned if the QM was still valid as the QM level was broken. In my opinion they are still valid QM's, We obviously would love every QM to be accurate to the pip, but this is not often the case. Taking a small drawdown can be expected sometimes at these levels.\n\nIn2forex","a":"in2forex","d":"","n":"#867","p":35,"im":[],"m":867},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_868","t":"Thx I2F for clearing that up. I've been using just that base (DBD or RBR) as the QM zone. However, i guess, looking at it in a HTF this definitely be valid. Makes sense to look at these zones in MTF and not have such strict rules for identifying these zones. Thanks for pointing it out:)","a":"astro","d":"","n":"#868","p":35,"im":[],"m":868},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_869","t":"There's this USDCHF QM taking place waiting for an FTR/FL to enter","a":"projectsagana","d":"","n":"#869","p":35,"im":[],"m":869},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_870","t":"projectsagana wrote: There's this USDCHF QM taking place waiting for an FTR/FL to enter\n\nUPDATE: so that QM did not work","a":"projectsagana","d":"","n":"#870","p":35,"im":[],"m":870},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_871","t":"astro wrote: I agree, Excellent QM examples JnrMFX.\n\nThe only 1 I\n\nwould question is your very first one. It looks like it may be a reaction to FL, rather than the QM level.\n\nThank's for your comment... that's exactly the point of my doubt.... i don't know where's my entry yet...... but now i can see the patterns.","a":"juniormaiafx","d":"","n":"#871","p":35,"im":["a639d21d2d766661ed83c3c0b4c97ef4090bdd16"],"m":871},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_872","t":"Here are an array of apparent QM's on the 15M for CJ. I also attached the HTF daily chart, which may seem to indicate a change in direction. More than open to feedback","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#872","p":35,"im":["8e4af61d10d896e754435d709f6b8408c85c34f5","60c70bbe78224a647c3599ebde05d11a2ec8d1a1"],"m":872},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_873","t":"Here is a current bullish one in the making on the GU. After a sustained down move, let's see where she wants to sail\n\nHere is a little image I use that helps me keep my H's, and L's straight.","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#873","p":35,"im":["29a9eac031a751cb04ec9c0b69353c5cdbfa10ce","24d05bd2c2563a598808e541c0113c18e1027e00"],"m":873},{"id":"quasimodo_p35_874","t":"SO, Back after a hiatus and losing my way.\n\nA valid QM?","a":"Mr Fish","d":"","n":"#874","p":35,"im":["1ba1cb7cbff67a71b289cb